    "carry_forward": [
      "A retraction is an edit plus a sweep. When correcting a claim asserted as verified, grep the whole document for every phrasing of it before returning: the body fix cost one extra implementer and one extra reviewer round here because the same claim survived in a Revision History bullet, which is the copy a skimmer reads.",
      "In a confirming reviewer round, name the current sealed documentation hash in the brief and tell the reviewer to read it rather than assume it matches the one already in his context. Each implementer correction re-seals the plan, so by the confirming round his first-read seal is stale; this cost a footer-only round twice in one loop.",
      "Ask the reviewer to audit the implementer's sweep rather than his fix. The fix is one line and checkable at a glance; the sweep is the claim that nothing else is stale, and it is where the third instance would hide."
    ],
    "closes_timestamp": "2026-09-28T23:27:48.301947+00:00",
